WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.060
Norway's wealth fund voted no on Musk's Tesla pay package for the second time. This is Tesla Shorts Time,

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:13.380
episode 679. German machine tools for optimus, the next inference chip, and robotaxi chargers

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:19.020
in Austin, then counterpoint and first principles. Norway's sovereign wealth fund, Bloomberg

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:29.980
reports, has consistently opposed that compensation package in prior Tesla shareholder votes. Tesla

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.900
the machine-tool maker EMAG, whose systems make drive components for humanoid robots.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:41.420
The deal is listed as an asset purchase, and EMAG has about 220 people at its saloxite

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:47.120
while planning to cut 300 jobs. Tesla is aiming for 1 million Optimus units a year

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:52.940
at Fremont, and up to 10 million at a future gigatexous line. The company recently set

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:58.120
up Tesla Machining Technologies Management SE, with its address at EMAG's headquarters.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:03.380
Germany has already supplied dozens of Optimus production sub-lines that were tested there

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:08.780
before shipment to Fremont, and production of the Optimus Gen 3 design has begun at Fremont

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:14.260
on floor space that used to build the Model S and Model X. Musk has said Tesla will likely

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:17.760
rent Optimus robots to customers rather than sell them outright.

00:01:18.777 --> 00:01:24.797
Next-generation AI-5 Inference Silicon, TipRanks reports, is not expected to enter production

00:01:24.797 --> 00:01:31.917
vehicles until 2028. That delay hits both unsupervised full-self driving, or FSD capability,

00:01:32.537 --> 00:01:36.517
and Optimus training and inference workloads that need higher performance silicon.

00:01:37.257 --> 00:01:42.837
Current HW-4 vehicles will keep running the existing end-to-end model until the new hardware arrives.

00:01:43.925 --> 00:01:49.785
Pawn Spring Service Center in Austin, not a Tesla app reports, is where Tesla submitted plans for

00:01:49.785 --> 00:01:54.545
16 fleet only V4 superchargers dedicated to the Robotaxi network.

00:01:54.825 --> 00:01:59.465
The site is meant to support the growing autonomous ride-hailing fleet operating in the Austin

00:01:59.465 --> 00:01:59.905
area.

00:02:00.884 --> 00:02:07.004
Tesla opened a 16-stall V4 station at Diocque Pyeong natural rest area, Drive Tesla Canada

00:02:07.004 --> 00:02:12.524
reports, on the Young-Dong Expressway with full 500 kilowatt cabinets on both sides of

00:02:12.524 --> 00:02:12.964
the highway.

00:02:13.604 --> 00:02:17.724
8-stalls serve traffic toward Inchon and 8-serve traffic toward Gangnam.

00:02:17.724 --> 00:02:24.484
The cabinet's support 400-volt to 1000-volt architectures, so 800-volt vehicles can charge

00:02:24.484 --> 00:02:25.424
at higher speeds.

00:02:25.924 --> 00:02:30.724
Magic dock adapters are built into every stall for non-Tesla CCS-1 vehicles.

00:02:31.244 --> 00:02:35.884
The station opened two days after General Motors announced its North American charging standard

00:02:35.884 --> 00:02:38.264
or NACS agreement for South Korea.

00:02:38.944 --> 00:02:44.944
Tesla is also preparing 500 kilowatt V4 sites in Canada, with construction underway in Quebec.

00:02:44.944 --> 00:02:52.765
General Motors GM Authority reports extended that NACS agreement with Tesla to cover vehicles sold in South Korea.

00:02:53.225 --> 00:02:58.645
The extension follows GM Korea's earlier commitment to adopt NACS ports on future models.

00:02:59.655 --> 00:03:06.455
A Powerwall owner, Yahoo Tech reports, found the system stops giving detailed electricity use data during grid outages,

00:03:06.875 --> 00:03:09.015
even when the home is running on battery power.

00:03:09.535 --> 00:03:14.435
The limitation shows up once the home is islanded and the owner tries to review consumption history.

00:03:14.435 --> 00:03:20.567
Cyber Truck Hardware, Torque News reports, is at the center of an owner debate over the 48

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:21.827
amp on-board charger.

00:03:22.547 --> 00:03:26.567
Owners are discussing whether to accelerate where so the charger fails in time for a

00:03:26.567 --> 00:03:32.387
warranty replacement, because waiting too long risks a $2500 repair bill once it is out

00:03:32.387 --> 00:03:32.887
of warranty.

00:03:33.865 --> 00:03:39.145
Tesla ended new orders for most cyber truck variants, BGR reports, and raised the cyber

00:03:39.145 --> 00:03:42.225
beast price to $114,990.

00:03:42.225 --> 00:03:47.725
dollars. Use Cybertruck listings have risen 10 to 15% in the months since that production

00:03:47.725 --> 00:03:55.105
wind down announcement. One New Jersey dealer is asking $150,790 for a low mileage cyber

00:03:55.105 --> 00:04:01.845
beast, $36,000 above the new vehicle price. Car Guru's data shows the average use Cybertruck

00:04:01.845 --> 00:04:10.545
at $89,715 after a 9.84% increase in the last 30 days. Count Tupes, denim, car, and

00:04:10.545 --> 00:04:17.025
ledges one reports, is the firm Tesla retained to handle federal solar policy lobbying in the United States.

00:04:17.645 --> 00:04:22.665
Duan Youngping, in a post T.S. Alamming carried, said he is now a Tesla shareholder.

00:04:23.205 --> 00:04:29.065
He once bet to Yuan that Tesla stock would be lower in 10 years. He said FSD has made his life

00:04:29.065 --> 00:04:34.645
noticeably more convenient. He also credited Starlink and Tesla vehicles with improving his daily

00:04:34.645 --> 00:04:43.305
experience. He took delivery of a top-spec Model S in 2013 for about $127,500. He registered

00:04:43.305 --> 00:04:51.041
the plate, W-E-T-S-L. Outside a sushi restaurant in Vancouver, CTV News reports and off-duty police

00:04:51.041 --> 00:04:56.741
officers Tesla struck and killed a pedestrian. Near-term gains now have to come from computers

00:04:56.741 --> 00:05:01.941
already paid for and already on the road, because the next board still has to pass a fabrication

00:05:01.941 --> 00:05:04.701
and qualification cycle, Tesla does not own.

00:05:05.341 --> 00:05:10.441
Hardware 4 was designed years earlier, and Tesla has kept feeding its software that sharpens

00:05:10.441 --> 00:05:13.441
perception and control without swapping the silicon.

00:05:14.041 --> 00:05:18.701
If that model keeps improving on today's accelerators, waiting on the next chip stops

00:05:18.701 --> 00:05:23.121
being a pure hardware countdown and becomes a question of how hard millions of deployed

00:05:23.121 --> 00:05:24.541
computers are being worked.

00:05:25.021 --> 00:05:30.141
Those units already have a cost, collected at the point of sale, so every extra increment

00:05:30.141 --> 00:05:35.121
of perception and control extracted from them raises the return on the installed base without a

00:05:35.121 --> 00:05:40.341
factory change. Tesla does control the training clusters and the vehicle software stack,

00:05:40.561 --> 00:05:45.601
which is why those updates can move without a new board. It cannot shorten the semi-conductor

00:05:45.601 --> 00:05:51.141
fabrication and qualification cycle that sits outside its walls, and that cycle will not compress

00:05:51.141 --> 00:05:56.641
just because cars and robots want the same inference parts. The practical result is getting more

00:05:56.641 --> 00:06:01.001
performance out of chips already shipping rather than from a generation that remains years

00:06:01.001 --> 00:06:01.341
away.

00:06:02.041 --> 00:06:04.521
A second constraint is mechanical, not digital.

00:06:05.161 --> 00:06:10.001
Humanoid drive systems need precision gears and actuators, and those machines set how

00:06:10.001 --> 00:06:15.041
many robots can be assembled each week once the Gen 3 design moves past the first low volume

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:15.401
runs.

00:06:16.061 --> 00:06:20.041
Pulling that machining in-house would put a production bottleneck under Tesla's roof

00:06:20.041 --> 00:06:24.701
instead of leaving it with a supplier whose own shop is shrinking, while demand for those

00:06:24.701 --> 00:06:29.921
specialized tools is rising. Compressing that supply chain is how weekly output can step

00:06:29.921 --> 00:06:33.181
up even while the next inference chip is still outside the building.

00:06:33.781 --> 00:06:38.321
The residential battery has a narrower gap and it is visibility rather than chemistry.

00:06:38.961 --> 00:06:46.441
Version 2026.44.3.1 already added manual battery pre-conditioning, which shows new controls

00:06:46.441 --> 00:06:51.741
can ride the same software pipe. The outage data path has not used that pipe, close

00:06:51.741 --> 00:06:55.841
it and an owner could see how much energy the system delivered while the grid was down

00:06:55.841 --> 00:07:01.321
and how state of charge moved minute by minute. Leave it closed and detailed home energy

00:07:01.321 --> 00:07:06.521
analytics stop at the edge of the grid connection. That hole is small and it keeps reappearing

00:07:06.521 --> 00:07:11.381
for anyone who relies on the wall for backup in places where weather takes the grid down.

